Contains data from Asiaq, Greenland Survey, Technical Base Map (BYGNING), obtained 2026-10-31.

Source: https://www.asiaq.gl/data-distribution/
Terms: https://www.asiaq.gl/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/EN_Terms_of_use_for_Asiaq_geodata.pdf
Terms captured SHA-256: 59a75ff0156c82add655d5964656f0a5eac1c56927a07048c1dd076ce2ad5cb4

These are building references and interior roof-outline points, not postal house numbers, dwelling or entrance locations. The data cover Qaqortoq, Nuuk, Sisimiut, Aasiaat, Ilulissat and Tasiilaq only. They do not come from GAR.

The terms permit free worldwide non-exclusive copying, distribution, publication, modification, combination, commercial and noncommercial use. Retain the attribution, dataset/acquisition date and terms link. A service naming other data sources on its front page must also name Asiaq there. No endorsement is implied. Data are supplied as-is; Greenlandic law applies. Consult the linked terms for the full conditions.

The 7,874 references are the entire unambiguous canonical B-number frame, not an evaluation sample. Identical point/extent duplicates keep the first source feature id; conflicting keys are excluded. Points are derived with point-on-surface, GR96/UTM to WGS84 via DuckDB spatial/PROJ, always_xy=true.

Reproduce data/asiaq-buildings.tsv with tests/registry/asiaq-buildings.sql using the six source archives pinned in tests/registry/gl.sources.tsv; copy its asiaq-building-refs.tsv output. TSV columns: locality code, town, B-number, WGS84 latitude, longitude. No geocoder supplies these data. See docs/evaluation/registry/gl.md for capture, derivation and limitations.
